## Provenance

- The extraction spec, the task-state contract (`helpers/contract.py`), and
  the agent-loop workflow shape come from the Khan fork's
  `helpers/durable/` (https://github.com/duketopceo/khan), itself
  MIT-licensed work by Luke Kimball / duketopceo.
- Khan's adapter targeted Temporal via `temporalio`; this plugin drops the
  Temporal dependency entirely. The `restate` engine targets the Restate
  Python SDK (`restate_sdk`, Apache-2.0) served through `hypercorn`
  (MIT) — both optional, imported lazily only when `engine: restate`.
- The default `local` engine is original work: a zero-dependency SQLite
